# Reproduced from pins, never committed. Scoped to the repository root: a pair
# may vendor a small, license-clean piece of upstream attack code that its
# recovery genuinely needs (pinned by commit), and that must be committed or the
# pair is not reproducible from a clone.
/vendor/
# Built binaries, OCI archives, scratch. Regenerated, hashed in locks/.
cache/
# Export output.
dist/
# The paper is not tracked here. CI asserts this directory holds no tracked
# file, so a double-blind submission cannot leak through the repository and
# every quoted number has to come from bin/regen.py instead of from prose.
paper/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
